  "boundaries": [
    "The transport responds after the heartbeat has recorded failure; detection depends on heartbeat intervals, database access and scheduling.",
    "The original exception is propagated. LeaseLost is not converted into a user stop intent.",
    "Existing epoch/version fences preserve replacement state and completed output; retired sessions and callbacks belong to the old cognition only.",
    "Expiry without replacement uses existing durable interruption and explicit resume behavior; healthy heartbeats continue to renew silent calls.",
    "Stopping a local model process does not prove service-side inference has stopped and does not undo earlier business effects.",
    "Browser timing about 997 ms uses an isolated 60-second waiting process and is not a production latency guarantee.",
    "Tests use actual local pipes and Store lease acquisition with fixed model outputs; no live model service, production data or publication."
